     "type": "text",
     "text": "{\"count\": 3, \"rationale\": \"crown:obtain is an OR of h3_0, h3_1 and h3_2, so all three must be cut. h3_2 can be cut either directly or by blocking all of h1_0, h1_1 and h2_2/h1_2, which is 3 nodes. If only h3_2 is blocked, h3_1 (fed by h1_0 or h2_2 via h1_2) and h3_0 (h1_2 AND h1_0) are still open, and no single extra block closes both. Blocking h3_2 plus any one other step leaves at least one route open, so 2 blocks are not enough. Blocking {h1_0, h1_1, h1_2} works: it removes h2_2, h3_0, h3_1 and h3_2. So the minimum is 3.\"}"
    }
